{"id":"c1054063-f411-4e53-85d5-9cee5451d1b8","object":"chat.completion","created":1784885719,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    import math\\n    # Validate case structure\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dict\\\")\\n    if 'threshold' not in case or 'calls' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must contain 'threshold' and 'calls'\\\")\\n    threshold = case['threshold']\\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"threshold must be a number\\\")\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n    \\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    \\n    for call in calls:\\n        # Validate each call\\n        if not isinstance(call, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"each call must be a dict\\\")\\n        required_fields = ['call_id', 'loss_without_call', 'loss_with_call', 'prediction_tokens', 'parseable']\\n        for field in required_fields:\\n            if field not in call:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"call missing field: {field}\\\")\\n        call_id = call['call_id']\\n        loss_without = call['loss_without_call']\\n        loss_with = call['loss_with_call']\\n        pred_tokens = call['prediction_tokens']\\n        parseable = call['parseable']\\n        \\n        # Validate types\\n        if not isinstance(call_id, str):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"call_id must be a string\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"loss_without_call must be a number\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"loss_with_call must be a number\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(pred_tokens, int) or pred_tokens <= 0:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"prediction_tokens must be a positive integer\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"parseable must be a boolean\\\")\\n        \\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / pred_tokens\\n        # Round to 8 decimal places\\n        normalized_gain = round(normalized_gain, 8)\\n        \\n        # Determine acceptance\\n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n        \\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            'accepted': accepted,\\n            'call_id': call_id,\\n            'normalized_gain': normalized_gain\\n        })\\n    \\n    return {\\n        'accepted_call_ids': accepted_call_ids,\\n        'diagnostics': diagnostics\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write Python code for solve(case) that implements the described task. The task is \"Agent-TF-01\". The output schema requires \"accepted_call_ids\" (array of strings) and \"diagnostics\" (array of objects with accepted, call_id, normalized_gain). The input payload has \"threshold\" and \"calls\", each call has call_id, loss_without_call, loss_with_call, prediction_tokens, parseable.\n\nFrom the description: \"For each call subtract loss with the call from loss without it.\" So gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call. \"Normalize gain by at least one prediction token.\" Means normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens? But it says \"by at least one prediction token\", maybe means divide by prediction_tokens, but if prediction_tokens is 0? But in fixtures, prediction_tokens are positive integers (2,4,5,6). So normalized_gain = (loss_without_call - loss_with_call) / prediction_tokens. Then \"Require both parseability and normalized gain at or above threshold.\" So accepted if parseable == true and normalized_gain >= threshold (the threshold from payload). The threshold is 0.05 in all fixtures.\n\n\"Keep diagnostics in supplied call order.\" So diagnostics list in same order as calls.\n\n\"Return accepted call IDs\" as list of strings.\n\n\"normalized_gain\" should be a number, presumably float. The output schema requires \"number\" type, so we can return float.\n\nAlso \"accepted\" boolean. For diagnostics, each call gets an entry, regardless of accepted? The schema: diagnostics array of objects with accepted, call_id, normalized_gain. So even if not accepted, we still include an entry with accepted=false and its normalized_gain. The description says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\". So should we round normalized_gain? It says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" in the mechanism boundary. But the output schema doesn't specify rounding. Probably we should round to some precision? The fixture payload values have many decimals. Possibly we should round to 8 decimal places? Or just keep as float? The requirement says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\". Let's interpret: The normalized_gain should be rounded to a reasonable number of decimal places, maybe 8 or as needed. But the output schema says \"type: number\", which in JSON can be any float. To be safe, we can round to, say, 8 decimal places to avoid floating point artifacts. But the spec says \"rounded\", so we should round. The examples in the candidate_artifact mention \"rounded per-call diagnostics\". I'll round to 8 decimal places.\n\nThe solve(case) should not mutate case.\n\nAlso \"Validate every required field before computing a result.\" So check that payload has 'threshold' and 'calls', each call has required fields. Raise ValueError if missing or invalid.\n\n\"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case instead of silently repairing it.\"\n\nImplementation: define solve(case) that returns dict with accepted_call_ids and diagnostics.\n\nEdge cases: prediction_tokens might be zero? But unlikely.\n\nNow, we need to output a JSON object with one key \"implementation\" whose value is a string of Python source code. The code must be escaped for JSON.\n\nWe'll write the solve function as a string.\n\nLet's produce the code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2171,"completion_tokens":1353,"total_tokens":3524,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":702},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":123},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}